"sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T05:48:20+00:00","id":"s812-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-03","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-03","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Veterans' Affairs."},"laws":[],"number":"812","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"S001217","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Scott, Rick [R-FL]","party":"R","state":"FL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-03","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p>This bill requires the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) to ensure that a veteran may obtain a physical copy of the form needed for travel reimbursements at any VA medical facility or, upon request, by mail. The VA must also ensure a veteran may submit the form to any VA medical facility in person or by mail. Such medical facilities must evaluate the form and process any claim associated with the form.</p>","updateDate":"2025-05-13T16:18:27Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"A bill to direct the Secretary of Veterans Affairs to ensure veterans may obtain a physical copy of a form for reimbursement of certain travel expenses by mail or at medical facilities of the Department of Veterans Affairs, and for other purposes.","type":"s","updateDate":"2025-07-15T10:56:25Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-07-15T10:56:25Z"}
